<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for ATKPlayer.app (Developer ID, outside the
  Mac App Store, so no App Sandbox). build-dmg.sh signs the executable with
  this file; verify-app.sh checks the signed copy matches it.

  It is deliberately empty. Each exception the hardened runtime offers was
  checked against what ATK Player does:

  com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation  NOT NEEDED
      Library validation only lets the process load code signed by the same
      team (or Apple). build-dmg.sh signs every bundled dylib, Qt framework
      and Qt plugin with the same identity as the app, and nothing is loaded
      from outside the bundle (the smoke test fails if it is).

  com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit
  com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory   NOT NEEDED
      FFmpeg runs precompiled code only, and its runtime CPU detection picks
      between functions already in the dylib. ATK Player is Qt Widgets with no
      QML or JavaScript engine, so there is no JIT either.

  com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables   NOT NEEDED
      Only the CI smoke test sets DYLD_PRINT_LIBRARIES, against the ad-hoc
      build; a released app needs no DYLD_* variables.

  com.apple.security.device.audio-input (microphone)
  com.apple.security.device.camera                     NOT NEEDED
      Audio is output only (QAudioSink); nothing records or captures. So there
      are no NSMicrophoneUsageDescription or NSCameraUsageDescription strings
      in Info.plist either.

  com.apple.security.automation.apple-events            NOT NEEDED
      Files and folders are opened through Launch Services
      (QDesktopServices::openUrl), not Apple Events.

  Network: the local API listens on 127.0.0.1. Network entitlements
  (com.apple.security.network.server/client) belong to the App Sandbox only;
  a hardened-runtime app outside the sandbox needs none.

  If a future feature needs one of these, add it here with its reason.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
